{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "LMR16006YQDDCTQ1",
 "kind": "switching_regulator",
 "manufacturer": "Texas Instruments",
 "title": "LMR16006Y-Q1 automotive 600 mA, 2.1 MHz step-down regulator with ECO mode",
 "source": {
  "revision": "SNVSAC1, June 2015",
  "pages": 24
 },
 "summary": "A 4 V to 40 V input (65 V transient) buck regulator for loads up to 600 mA, with an integrated high-side MOSFET, fixed 2.1 MHz peak current mode control, and internal compensation and soft-start. In light-load ECO mode it draws 28 µA from the input; in shutdown, 1 µA. It comes as an adjustable version (0.765 V feedback) and fixed 3.3 V and 5 V versions in a 6-pin SOT-23-THIN, qualified to AEC-Q100 Grade 1.",
